  "status": "published",
  "title": "Trump Says He Convinced Nvidia to Bring Back Its CEO. What Did the Board Hear?",
  "deck": "Nvidia says senior U.S. officials gave it input before directors unanimously reinstated Jensen Huang. The company’s filing fixes the date of the decision. Its public statement leaves the substance of that advice largely undisclosed.",
  "category": "economy",
  "categoryLabel": "Economy",
  "type": "article",
  "author": "EP News",
  "publishedAt": "2026-11-25T12:31:48Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-11-25T12:31:48Z",
  "body": [
    "Donald Trump says he spoke to Nvidia’s board and persuaded it to bring back Jensen Huang. Nvidia confirms that its directors received input from senior U.S. officials before voting unanimously to reinstate the chipmaker’s co-founder. Its announcement gives the board’s conclusion on national security but leaves out who provided the government’s assessment and the evidence behind it. [CNBC interview](https://pressroom.versantmedia.com/cnbc/press-releases/cnbc-transcript-president-donald-trump-speaks-cnbcs-eamon-javers-and-squawk) · [Nvidia announcement](https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director/)",
    "## What Trump says he told the board",
    "In the Nov. 23 CNBC interview, Trump said he spoke to directors and convinced them. Asked whether he personally called into the board meeting, he said he was represented at the meeting and declined to say whom he spoke to. He said a government review had cleared Huang personally and argued that losing Huang’s expertise would pose a greater risk to the United States. [CNBC interview](https://pressroom.versantmedia.com/cnbc/press-releases/cnbc-transcript-president-donald-trump-speaks-cnbcs-eamon-javers-and-squawk)",
    "Trump also told CNBC he had urged Nvidia to continue checking its compliance with U.S. export controls. His support for bringing Huang back came as Washington was tightening restrictions on some advanced-chip shipments and scrutinizing whether chips were reaching China through other markets. [Reuters](https://www.reuters.com/technology/nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-ceo-2026-11-23/)",
    "## What Nvidia put on the record",
    "Nvidia’s filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission says directors reinstated Huang as president, chief executive and a board member on Nov. 22, a day before the company announced the decision. In the announcement, Nvidia said directors met with Huang and were satisfied with his candor and ability to lead. It separately said government input left the board confident that reinstating him posed no national security risk. [SEC filing](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000090/nvda-20261122.htm) · [Nvidia announcement](https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director/)",
    "The vote reversed the position board chair Harvey Jones had expressed less than a week earlier. Reuters reported that Jones had ruled out returning Huang to the CEO job because his personal conduct was inconsistent with Nvidia’s code. The company had already announced that its board was opening an independent inquiry into reporting that Huang had been targeted by a foreign intelligence effort. Reuters reported that the company’s investigation was still unfinished when he returned. [Nvidia’s Nov. 8 statement](https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/statement-from-nvidia-board-of-directors) · [Reuters](https://www.reuters.com/technology/nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-ceo-2026-11-23/)",
    "## The next public questioning",
    "The Senate Banking Committee lists Huang as the witness at a Dec. 3 hearing on U.S. export controls. Senators can ask what assurances Nvidia received, how the board assessed them, and what oversight the company has in place to keep restricted chips from reaching unauthorized buyers. [Senate hearing notice](https://www.banking.senate.gov/hearings/protecting-americas-ai-advantage-oversight-of-us-export-controls)"
  ],
